    "intro_html":  "Stifado is the Greek stew where the onions are not a background note, they are half the dish. They cook down until they melt into a sweet and sour braise sharpened with red wine vinegar and warmed with allspice and nutmeg. Beef chuck goes in tough and comes out shredding. Each bowl carries {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
